[FINDING]
  The plan sheet carries, AS POSITIONED OBJECTS: STA callouts (x,y), numeric AP labels
  (x,y), FLOWER POT / SPLICE / TERMINAL PORT text, AND a dense vector layer (lines+curves
  = leader lines + bored-run polylines; rects = structure symbols). The station<->structure
  association is a SPATIAL nearest-label / leader-line join — which linear text-order
  extraction discards. The hand-built BRENHAM_PH5_RUN_ENDPOINTS table is exactly this join
  done by eye. Extraction primitive = position-aware 'STA-callout -> nearest structure
  label (or leader-line-connected label)' on each sheet, validated against the known AP
  run-ends, then joined to the Target #25 AP/structure index for geometry.
